  Object.assign(charContent,{
    'beatrix-kiddo':{
      journey:`<p>The Bride's ISTJ profile is Kill Bill's most precisely constructed revenge narrative: the Si dominant that has accumulated the comprehensive record of what was taken - the wedding, the husband, the child, the life - and the Te that cannot rest until every outstanding item in that record has been addressed. She does not pursue the Deadly Viper Assassination Squad from passion or ideology. She pursues them because the Si library contains the record of what each specific person did, and the Te cannot close a library entry that has not been resolved. They are outstanding obligations. The ISTJ does not leave outstanding obligations.</p><p>Her training - under Pai Mei, the years in Japan, the comprehensive physical preparation - is the Te implementing the Si library's most demanding requirement: what the resolution of this specific record will require is this specific level of capability. She builds it. The training is not impressive to her. It is necessary. The distinction is the type.</p><p>Her relationship with BB is the inferior Ne's most complete operation: the specific possibility that the Si library had not contained - the child survived, the child is alive, the child can be recovered - arriving at the exact moment when the Te's programme had been running for years without the inferior function having generated this alternative. The alternative overrides the programme. The ISTJ whose most foundational Si entry has been revised does not need to complete the programme. She takes BB and goes. The library entry that supersedes all others has been updated.</p>`,
      mistype:`<p>The Bride is sometimes typed INTJ - the comprehensive plan, the long-range patience, the apparent strategic intelligence of the revenge operation. But INTJ's Ni synthesises a vision and builds toward it. The Bride's programme is Si-accumulated: she has the record of what each person did and the Te implementing the resolution of each record entry in sequence. She does not have a vision of how the overall project ends. She has a list. The list determines the sequence. The Te implements each item. That list-and-sequence operation is Si-Te, not Ni-Te.</p><p>The ESTP argument comes from her physical dominance and present-tense combat excellence. But ESTP responds to the present situation. The Bride prepares for each encounter in advance, through training and intelligence, and the combat is the Te implementing the prepared capability against the anticipated configuration. She does not read the Crazy 88 and improvise. She trained for ten years to be capable of the Crazy 88. The preparation is Si-Te. The combat is the implementation.</p><p>The clincher is the list. She crosses names off with a marker. That list is the Si library's outstanding obligations rendered visible, and the crossing-off is the Te's most complete available expression of what resolution means to the dominant function: the record is closed, the obligation is discharged, the entry is marked complete. She crosses off O-Ren. She crosses off Vernita. She gets to Bill. The list drives the entire film. That is ISTJ.</p>`
    },

    'homer-simpson':{
      journey:`<p>Homer Simpson's ESFP profile is The Simpsons' most precisely calibrated comic construction: the Se dominant reading every available present moment for the most enjoyable immediately available option, the Fi endorsing the option with total investment, and the inferior Ni providing exactly the minimum forecast required to occasionally identify that the option will cause a problem after the fact. He does not choose the donut over the diet for strategic reasons. The Se identifies the donut and the Fi endorses it before the inferior function has had time to generate the consequence. The consequence arrives. Homer deals with it in the next present moment.</p><p>His love for Marge is the inferior Ni's most consistent and most surprising operation: across decades of disasters, schemes, and consequences the inferior function failed to forecast in advance, the specific person accumulates in the inferior function with a weight that the dominant function's perpetual present-tense engagement cannot displace. He does not choose Marge from strategic assessment or values-based conviction. He keeps coming back to Marge because the inferior function has built the record and the record is non-negotiable, even for a man whose dominant function cannot sustain attention on anything for longer than it takes to consume a donut.</p><p>"D'oh!" is the inferior function's most complete self-assessment: the Se identified the opportunity, the Fi endorsed it, the inferior Ni has now arrived with the forecast that was unavailable at the moment of the decision. The time delay between the decision and the forecast is the type's most characteristic comedic quality, and thirty-plus seasons have demonstrated that the delay is structural rather than correctable.</p>`,
      mistype:`<p>Homer is sometimes typed ESFJ - the family warmth, the apparent care for Marge and the kids, the social orientation. But ESFJ's Fe is dominant: it reads the group and responds to the group's emotional reality. Homer does not read the group. He encounters the group in the present moment and the Fi endorses whatever the group's present-tense configuration requires from him, usually after some delay. The difference is the Fe's continuous attunement versus the ESFP's periodic present-tense engagement.</p><p>The ESTP argument comes from his apparent tactical intelligence in specific episodes. But ESTP is Se-Ti: the present-tense reading analytically evaluated. Homer's Ti rarely produces adequate evaluation before the Se has already committed to the option the Fi endorsed. The intelligence arrives after the commitment. That post-commitment intelligence is the inferior function's most common expression in the show.</p><p>The clincher is the monorail. He becomes the monorail conductor because the Se identified the most exciting available present-tense role and the Fi endorsed it completely before the Ti or the inferior Ni produced any assessment of whether being a monorail conductor was viable. The monorail crashes. He saves everyone. He moves on to the next present moment. That sequence - commitment before assessment, survival through present-tense improvisation, immediate departure to the next available excitement - is the ESFP function stack at its most complete.</p>`
    },
    'bart-simpson':{
      journey:`<p>Bart Simpson's ESTP profile is The Simpsons' most complete portrait of the type in its most developmentally unconstrained form: the Se reading every available social situation for the most interesting available prank, the Ti evaluating each prank's technical requirements, and the inferior Ni providing exactly zero forecast of what the prank produces for the specific person who receives it until the prank has been executed and the consequence is visible. He does not prank Skinner from malice. He pranks Skinner because the Se has identified the most interesting available angle on the principal's specific vulnerabilities and the Ti has confirmed the angle is technically viable.</p><p>His relationship with Milhouse is the inferior Fe at its most complete expression: the specific person who the inferior function has designated as the primary relational investment, held with the completeness the inferior function provides for the few things it fully endorses. He treats Milhouse badly in episodes. He defends Milhouse in others. The inferior function's investment is real and it is inconsistent, which is the inferior function's most honest relationship to the things it values.</p><p>His eventual arc toward not-being-Bart - the dreams of being a lawyer, the moments of genuine warmth with Homer, the small acts of actual responsibility - is the inferior Ni finally generating enough forecast to hold the present-tense action against a picture of future consequences that the dominant function can use. He does not become a different person. He becomes the ESTP who has developed the inferior function enough to occasionally weigh the prank against what comes after.</p>`,
      mistype:`<p>Bart is sometimes typed ENFP - the apparent enthusiasm, the warmth, the relational quality of his most significant moments. But ENFP's Ne generates possibilities about what could be. Bart identifies what is present and finds the most interesting available angle on it. He does not imagine what Skinner could become or what the school could be. He reads the specific vulnerability and deploys the specific prank. That identification-and-deployment is Se-Ti, not Ne-Fi.</p><p>The ISTP argument comes from his technical competence and the apparent interiority. But ISTP is Ti-dominant: the framework precedes the engagement. Bart's Ti follows his Se. He does not build frameworks for pranking Skinner in advance; he reads Skinner, identifies the angle, and the Ti evaluates the identified angle's feasibility. The Se is primary. The Ti is secondary. That direction is ESTP.</p><p>The clincher is "Eat my shorts." That is the Se dominant's relationship to the authority structure: the reading is complete (this specific person is asserting this specific authority in this specific way), the Ti has identified the most economical available response (non-compliance expressed in minimum viable terms), and the inferior Ni has not been consulted about what the response produces. The punchline is delivered. The consequence arrives. Bart is surprised every time. That structural surprise - the inferior function's arrival - is the ESTP's most complete relationship to its own operation.</p>`
    },

    'peeta-mellark':{
      journey:`<p>Peeta Mellark's ENFJ profile is The Hunger Games' most complete portrait of the type in the most demanding available context: the person whose Fe dominant reads the arena, the Capitol audiences, and the specific people around him with total accuracy, and who uses that accuracy not to survive but to build the conditions in which the person the Fe has designated as primary can survive. He does not compete in the Hunger Games. He manages the public's relationship to Katniss while she manages the arena's physical demands. The division is the ENFJ's most honest possible relationship to what it cannot do: the Fe provides what the INTJ's Ni-Te cannot generate, and the INTJ provides what the ENFJ's Fe cannot build alone.</p><p>His brainwashing - the hijacking, the mutt-tracker venom, the false memories - is the ENFJ's most specific vulnerability rendered literal: the Fe that reads people by receiving their emotional reality has been given false emotional reality to read. He is not brainwashed into hating Katniss. He is given false memories that produce the experience of genuine feeling about those memories. The ENFJ cannot distinguish between genuine feeling and the feeling produced by false inputs, because the dominant function's operation does not have an accuracy-verification layer. It receives. When the reception is corrupted, the reading is corrupted.</p><p>His recovery - "Real or not real?" - is the inferior Ti finally being deployed as the verification mechanism the dominant function cannot provide on its own. He cannot trust his own emotional reception. He asks Katniss to verify. That asking is the ENFJ discovering the inferior function's most specific available use: not as an analytical engine but as a reality-check for the dominant function's most complete vulnerability.</p>`,
      mistype:`<p>Peeta is sometimes typed ISFJ - the apparent care, the quiet loyalty, the service orientation. But ISFJ's Si is dominant: it operates from accumulated precedent. Peeta's most significant acts are all Ni-generated: he saw where Katniss's arc was pointing before she did, synthesised the public narrative that would protect her, and built the performance around the synthesis. He did not follow an existing template; he generated the correct approach from the reading the Fe provided.</p><p>The INFJ argument comes from his apparent visionary quality. But INFJ's Ni is primary: the synthesis precedes the engagement. Peeta leads with Fe: the reading of the specific person is primary, and the Ni synthesises the long-range picture from what the reading produces. He loved Katniss first. The strategy followed. That love-first sequence is ENFJ.</p><p>The clincher is the cave. He tells the love story to the Hunger Games audience not because the Ni synthesised that it was strategically optimal (INTJ/INFJ) or because the Te assessed it as institutionally appropriate (ESTJ). He tells it because the Fe has been holding this specific truth about this specific person for years, the arena provided the conditions for the expression, and the Ni immediately synthesised that the expression would simultaneously serve Katniss's survival. The love and the strategy are inseparable because for the ENFJ they are the same operation.</p>`
    },
    'abby-anderson':{
      journey:`<p>Abby Anderson's ISTJ profile is The Last of Us Part II's most demanding character study: the specific obligation, accumulated across years of loss, implemented with the comprehensive capability the Te has built in preparation, at maximum cost to every relationship the inferior function had been accumulating simultaneously. She kills Joel not from savagery but from the Si library's most complete outstanding entry: her father died, the person who killed him is identified, the outstanding obligation requires resolution. The Te implements the resolution. The Si closes the entry. What follows is the cost the inferior function was accumulating in parallel.</p><p>Her relationship with Owen and Mel, with the Wolves, with Lev and Yara: the inferior Ne and inferior Fi finding, while the Te's primary programme was running, the specific people the inferior functions have designated as worth protecting. The game is the ISTJ discovering that the Si library has entries the Te's primary programme was not accounting for - the specific people who were accumulating alongside the obligation. When the programme's implementation destroys those entries, the library requires revision.</p><p>Her eventual choice - releasing Ellie in the water, refusing to complete the final kill - is the Si library's most complete revision: the Ellie entry has accumulated sufficient weight to override the Joel entry's completion requirement. She does not forgive Ellie. She recognises that the outstanding obligations in the Lev entry, which require her survival for their resolution, supersede the Joel entry's remaining implementation steps. The ISTJ's most precise moral calculation: which outstanding obligations are more outstanding.</p>`,
      mistype:`<p>Abby is sometimes typed ENTJ - the physical dominance, the apparent strategic management of the Wolves operation, the command presence. But ENTJ builds toward a Ni vision. Abby's operation is Te implementing the Si library's outstanding obligations. She did not build a vision of what the post-Joel world would look like. She built the capability to resolve the outstanding entry. The capability and the resolution: Si-Te, not Ni-Te.</p><p>The ISTP argument comes from her physical competence, the precision of the combat. But ISTP is Ti dominant: the analytical framework precedes the engagement. Abby's physical capability is Si-accumulated: years of training, building the specific capability the record of her father's death identified as required. The capability was built from the library's entry, not from Ti analysis of what the encounter would require.</p><p>The clincher is the aquarium. She goes back for Lev. The Te's primary programme is complete. The Si library has no remaining outstanding obligation from the Joel entry. The inferior function's entries - Lev, Yara, Owen, Mel - have been accumulating across the full duration of the primary programme's implementation. The aquarium is the ISTJ discovering that the inferior function's accumulated entries are, collectively, the outstanding obligation that supersedes everything else in the library. She goes back. That return is Si-Te completing the more fundamental outstanding obligation.</p>`
    },
    'nucky-thompson':{
      journey:`<p>Nucky Thompson's INTJ profile is Boardwalk Empire's most complete portrait of the type when the Te has been running the Atlantic City operation for decades and the Ni synthesis has finally produced the verdict that the structure was built on a specific early act that the inferior function never fully processed. His relationship with Jimmy Darmody - the apprentice he mentored and then had killed - is not a strategic error or a personal failing. It is the INTJ's most specific vulnerability: the inferior Fe had made the specific investment, the Te implemented the elimination as required by the Ni synthesis's assessment of Jimmy's threat, and the inferior function's record of the investment does not close when the Te closes the person.</p><p>His arc across six seasons is the Ni synthesis running its most honest available operation: the Te builds the institution, the institution requires decisions that cost the inferior function its most complete available investments, and the Ni keeps synthesising the same conclusion - power requires the specific elimination of the specific attachment - until the inferior function's accumulated weight finally produces a verdict the Ni cannot override. He did not start Boardwalk Empire as a bad man. He became one through the consistent application of the INTJ's most reliable failure mode: the Te implementing the Ni's requirements without the inferior function having been given adequate input into what each implementation cost.</p><p>His death - shot by the grown child of the specific woman his early choices destroyed - is the Ni synthesis's most honest final operation: the framework accounts for everything except the specific costs of its own implementation, and the specific costs eventually arrive in the form of the specific people those costs produced.</p>`,
      mistype:`<p>Nucky is sometimes typed ENTJ - the institutional management, the visible authority, the comprehensive command of Atlantic City's political machine. But ENTJ builds outward and inhabits institutional leadership naturally. Nucky manages from concealment: the public face is the Atlantic City treasurer, the actual operation is managed from the private synthesis. That concealment - the INTJ whose framework runs beneath the institutional surface - distinguishes him from the ENTJ who inhabits the institution directly.</p><p>The ISTJ argument comes from his apparent institutional loyalty, the conservative management style. But ISTJ operates from accumulated precedent. Nucky consistently violates every available institutional precedent - Prohibition, Volstead, the political alliances - because the Ni synthesis has determined what the operation requires and the Te implements it regardless of institutional constraint. He is not maintaining anything. He is building what the synthesis requires and dismantling what the synthesis has assessed as surplus.</p><p>The clincher is his relationship with Margaret. He married her for reasons the Ni synthesis identified as operationally correct and the inferior Fe found genuinely compelling simultaneously. He could not separate the calculation from the feeling. The INTJ whose inferior function has made a specific investment that the Te simultaneously assesses as operationally useful: the two operations run in parallel without the type having adequate access to which one is primary. Margaret eventually left because she finally determined which one was primary. Nucky never could.</p>`
    }
  });


