      mistype:`<p>Holiday is sometimes typed INFP - the apparent interior depth, the personal quality of her phrasing, the values-driven quality of Strange Fruit. But INFP leads with Fi and follows with Ne: the interior is primary and the Ne generates the expression. Holiday's expression is Se-grounded: the specific voice, the specific physical delivery, the specific present-tense inhabitation of each note. She is not generating the expression from the interior. She is expressing the interior through the body's most complete available present-tense instrument. That body-first expression is ISFP.</p><p>The ESFP argument comes from the apparent social engagement, the performance presence. But ESFP is Se dominant: the present moment is primary and the Fi provides the personal warmth. Holiday's Fi is dominant: the specific assessment of what each lyric actually contains is primary, and the Se delivers the assessment through the voice. When the Se delivers something the Fi has not endorsed, the result is empty. She could not sing a lyric she did not believe. That endorsement requirement is Fi dominant.</p><p>The clincher is her insistence on performing Strange Fruit against record label pressure. The Se had delivered the song with the Fi's complete assessment of what it contained. The exterior world - the label, the venues - required her not to perform it. The Fi dominant's assessment was that the song's content was non-negotiable. The Se delivered it anyway. That insistence - the interior's assessment overriding the exterior world's institutional requirements - is the ISFP's most defining quality.</p>`
