      mistype:`<p>Bukowski is sometimes typed ISTP or ISFP depending on which poems are being read. The ISFP argument comes from the apparent warmth of the specific moments, the depth of feeling in the best work. But ISFP is Fi dominant: the values are primary and generate the Se expression. Bukowski's most defining quality is the Ti framework's most precise available assessment of what the specific life actually contains, delivered without the Fi's mediation of the assessment's social acceptability. He is not expressing the interior's warmth. He is delivering the Ti's most accurate available verdict on the specific configuration.</p><p>The ENTP argument comes from the range of his engagement and the apparent pleasure in the verbal sparring. But ENTP generates possibilities and finds the exploration energising. Bukowski's engagement is Se-primary: the specific present-tense configuration, inhabited completely, assessed by the Ti, and delivered through the poem before the inferior function has had time to produce the social management that would have prevented the delivery.</p><p>The clincher is his response to rejection. He collected rejection slips in a box and continued submitting. The Ti framework had assessed the work as correct - internally consistent with the most precise available framework for what the specific life actually contained - and the exterior world's assessment was insufficient grounds for revising the Ti's verdict. He continued. The Ti was primary. The exterior world's response was secondary data.</p>`
