      mistype:`<p>Picasso is sometimes typed ENTP - the apparent intellectual pleasure in the conceptual, the range of his periods, the Ne-quality of his perpetual innovation. But ENTP generates possibilities about what art could be. Picasso reads what art actually is at each specific present-tense moment and the Ti assesses the most interesting available angle. He is not exploring the possibilities of representation. He is reading the specific present-tense reality and finding the most precise available instrument for what the reading actually contains. The reading precedes the concept. The ENTP would have started with the concept.</p><p>The INTJ argument comes from the comprehensive model - the periods, the apparent systematic progression through available styles. But INTJ builds Ni syntheses. Picasso reads each specific present-tense configuration and the Ti assesses the most interesting available angle. The periods are the accumulated record of what each specific present-tense configuration of the available artistic context produced when the Ti processed it with maximum fidelity. The progression is iterative, not convergent.</p><p>The clincher is his portrait of Gertrude Stein. He repainted the face eighty times. Each repainting was the Se reading the specific present-tense configuration of the specific face and the Ti finding the most interesting available angle that the prior painting had not yet produced. He stopped when the Ti's assessment was complete. The face in the final painting does not look like Gertrude Stein. It looks like what the Ti determined was the most precise available representation of what the Se had been reading across eighty sessions. She said it did not look like her. He said it would.</p>`
