    'daft-punk':{letters:`<div class="letter-block">
  <div class="letter-display"><span class="letter-big">I</span><span class="letter-word">Introverted</span></div>
  <p>Daft Punk were among music's most profoundly private artists, hiding behind robot helmets and refusing the celebrity machinery with a consistency that shaped their entire identity. They avoided interviews, declined to show their faces, and processed their artistic vision through years of secluded studio work, producing their albums in the extended private labor of a duo whose real existence happened behind the masks and inside the studio.</p>
  <p>Their art depended on sustained private creative labor. Daft Punk developed their albums through years of meticulous, secluded production work, drew their sonic vision from deep interior engagement with their material, and offered the results to the world through the impersonal interface of the helmets. That reclusive, studio-dwelling, privately-creating depth, the duo whose true identity was always behind the masks, is the introversion at the heart of their project.</p>
</div>
<div class="letter-block">
  <div class="letter-display"><span class="letter-big">N</span><span class="letter-word">iNtuitive</span></div>
  <p>Daft Punk were visionary electronic musicians who anticipated the future of their genre with remarkable foresight. They perceived where electronic music was heading before their peers, pioneered the fusion of electronic production with live instrumentation and pop songcraft that would shape the next generation, and built each album as a unified conceptual vision rather than a collection of tracks. They saw further than their contemporaries.</p>
  <p>Their imagination worked at the level of long-range sonic vision and conceptual architecture. Daft Punk conceived each project as a total artistic vision, the anime narrative of Discovery, the live-instrument recording experiment of Random Access Memories, perceiving the larger pattern of what electronic music could become and building their albums toward futures they were the first to hear. That visionary, conceptual, future-anticipating imagination is the intuition driving their foundational work.</p>
</div>
<div class="letter-block">
  <div class="letter-display"><span class="letter-big">T</span><span class="letter-word">Thinking</span></div>
  <p>Daft Punk operated through rigorous, meticulous, technically exacting sonic craft. Their production was legendary for its precision, their attention to sonic detail obsessive, and their approach to the recording process reflected the analytical rigor of minds that treated music-making as a disciplined engineering problem. The perfectionism was the perfectionism of a technical intelligence pursuing the exact sound they had decided on.</p>
  <p>Their creative process was analytically structured and results-driven. Daft Punk approached their albums through systematic technical experimentation, pursued their sonic vision through rigorous analytical attention to production detail, and held their work to standards of technical precision that reflected a fundamentally logical and structurally-analyzing creative intelligence. That meticulous, technically-rigorous, analytically-deployed craft is the thinking function at their core.</p>
</div>
<div class="letter-block">
  <div class="letter-display"><span class="letter-big">J</span><span class="letter-word">Judging</span></div>
  <p>Daft Punk were supreme perfectionist craftsmen who pursued their artistic vision with iron patient discipline. They spent years on each album, held every detail to exacting standards, and committed absolutely to the decided vision for each project, refusing to release work until it met the precise standard they had set. The long gaps between albums reflected the iron discipline of artists who would not compromise their decided vision.</p>
  <p>Their career was the sustained decided execution of a series of meticulously controlled artistic visions. Daft Punk committed fully to each project, organized their creative process around the patient long-term pursuit of their decided sonic goals, and maintained through decades the unwavering commitment to craft and concept that defined them. That patient, decided, vision-executing discipline, the duo whose perfectionism was the core of their identity, is the judging function behind their enduring influence.</p>
</div>`,journey:`<p>Daft Punk emerged from the French house scene in the mid-1990s as a duo whose distinctive fusion of electronic dance music with pop melody and conceptual ambition quickly set them apart from their peers. Their early work established them as sonic innovators, and the decision to perform and appear exclusively in robot helmets, concealing their faces permanently, established the anonymous, concept-driven identity that would define their entire career.</p><p>Their albums were spaced across years, each one a distinct conceptual vision developed through meticulous private studio work. Discovery wove electronic music into an anime narrative of staggering ambition, and Random Access Memories pushed the project further by recording with live musicians in pursuit of a warmer, more human electronic sound that influenced the entire next generation of producers. Each album anticipated where the genre was heading before anyone else heard it.</p><p>They disbanded in 2021 with a characteristically wordless farewell video, ending a career whose influence on electronic and popular music had been profound and whose anonymous, perfectionist, concept-driven identity had redefined what an electronic act could be. Their arc is the sustained, meticulous, visionary career of a pair of anonymous sonic architects whose iron perfectionism, conceptual ambition, and reclusive creative discipline gave electronic music some of its most influential and enduring recordings.</p>`,mistype:`<p>The common alternative is INTP, because Daft Punk were brilliant analytical sonic innovators. But Daft Punk were supreme perfectionist craftsmen who committed absolutely to decided artistic visions, spending years on each album and refusing to release work until it met their exact standard. Their creativity was pursued through iron decided discipline, not open-ended exploration. That patient, decided, vision-executing perfectionism is the INTJ rather than the more open INTP.</p><p>INFP gets suggested for the conceptual depth and artistic sensitivity. But Daft Punk operated through rigorous, meticulous, technically exacting sonic craft, pursuing their vision through analytical attention to production detail and systematic technical experimentation rather than warm personal feeling. Their engine was technical precision. That meticulous, analytically-deployed craft is the INTJ.</p>`},
